[[:db/retract 17592186118388 :answer-field/choices 17592186118389] [:db/retract 17592186118388 :answer-field/choices 17592186118390] [:db/retract 17592186118388 :answer-field/choices 17592186118391] [:db/retract 17592186118388 :answer-field/choices 17592186118392] [:db/retract 17592186118388 :answer-field/choices 17592186118393] [:db/retract 17592186246741 :answer-field/choices 17592186244766] [:db/retract 17592186344579 :answer-field/choices 17592186342309] [:db/retract 17592186318899 :answer-field/choices 17592186318047] {:db/id 17592186119820 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8a5b5cd1-19ba-524a-960c-18e8a17d885d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119821 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7fd80750-80bf-5e1d-b08d-abec51a32d9d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119632 :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n![](images/e5/e5b57b4f1488c927d64d89cb4352715b471025a111a39fe786c869973401fbd4.svg)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix above corresponds to the following system of equations: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2 =-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1 + 3 \\left( -1 \\right)  = -5\n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad\nx_1 = -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/28/286b19d6c3b5b3fac7f65ffd4adab1b175d4dab5fab1e5bb7a85da692f09224a.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119633 :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above system as an augmented matrix $M$ and reducing using Gaussian elimination, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -9{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=7 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3}=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 =2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-9x_2 - 2 = 7 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_2=-1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+3(-1) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1 = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/76/766d220a3c5bc2819ab05886751b6a1b782ece06c9d71b9baaaee19e9a2ecbdd.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-8a5b5cd1-19ba-524a-960c-18e8a17d885d" :question/id #uuid "8a5b5cd1-19ba-524a-960c-18e8a17d885d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112202" :question/problem "Find the vector $x$, if $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,-3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0e865a75-dfdd-5a58-b928-640a4073b739"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0e865a75-dfdd-5a58-b928-640a4073b739" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e865a75-dfdd-5a58-b928-640a4073b739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b1937a48-91af-551c-9a98-39c8335585e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e60504c0-156d-5be5-b8b0-a6c50751ba29" "answer-b1937a48-91af-551c-9a98-39c8335585e6" "answer-f9aaf9bb-e91f-5b1b-81ad-71ec2b8c9df5" "answer-2ce43d07-7d46-5c98-b744-3a88ad395201" "answer-d52b898d-8b0d-5322-b32b-d790188a0c69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e60504c0-156d-5be5-b8b0-a6c50751ba29" :answer/id #uuid "e60504c0-156d-5be5-b8b0-a6c50751ba29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-23 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1937a48-91af-551c-9a98-39c8335585e6" :answer/id #uuid "b1937a48-91af-551c-9a98-39c8335585e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9aaf9bb-e91f-5b1b-81ad-71ec2b8c9df5" :answer/id #uuid "f9aaf9bb-e91f-5b1b-81ad-71ec2b8c9df5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ce43d07-7d46-5c98-b744-3a88ad395201" :answer/id #uuid "2ce43d07-7d46-5c98-b744-3a88ad395201" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d52b898d-8b0d-5322-b32b-d790188a0c69" :answer/id #uuid "d52b898d-8b0d-5322-b32b-d790188a0c69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120379 :question/problem "Find the vector $x$, if $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,-3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,5\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}25 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 21 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118388 :answer-field/correct "answer-d3e2768b-1c0b-587c-8548-9c3d0f3aae84" :answer-field/choices ["answer-29376ce5-1709-5e3d-9b46-93794cef8b6b" "answer-916a198b-9533-5031-bb1d-8a1a6d13d6a1" "answer-2513b831-2bda-5222-a175-9dbc2cbe0fa3" "answer-54390e6e-dcb1-5dd3-95c7-15b36777dc0f" "answer-d3e2768b-1c0b-587c-8548-9c3d0f3aae84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29376ce5-1709-5e3d-9b46-93794cef8b6b" :answer/id #uuid "29376ce5-1709-5e3d-9b46-93794cef8b6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-916a198b-9533-5031-bb1d-8a1a6d13d6a1" :answer/id #uuid "916a198b-9533-5031-bb1d-8a1a6d13d6a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2513b831-2bda-5222-a175-9dbc2cbe0fa3" :answer/id #uuid "2513b831-2bda-5222-a175-9dbc2cbe0fa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-21 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54390e6e-dcb1-5dd3-95c7-15b36777dc0f" :answer/id #uuid "54390e6e-dcb1-5dd3-95c7-15b36777dc0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3e2768b-1c0b-587c-8548-9c3d0f3aae84" :answer/id #uuid "d3e2768b-1c0b-587c-8548-9c3d0f3aae84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 21 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247250 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186246741 :answer-field/choices ["answer-dbad1c26-6ccc-544d-abe3-93664ba57768"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbad1c26-6ccc-544d-abe3-93664ba57768" :answer/id #uuid "dbad1c26-6ccc-544d-abe3-93664ba57768" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345146 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-7fd80750-80bf-5e1d-b08d-abec51a32d9d" :question/id #uuid "7fd80750-80bf-5e1d-b08d-abec51a32d9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112213" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 40\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -10{x}_{2}=40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(-4)=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1d8ec2ef-2c05-5932-bd6d-c9b93200f648"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1d8ec2ef-2c05-5932-bd6d-c9b93200f648" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d8ec2ef-2c05-5932-bd6d-c9b93200f648" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8680e3ab-ac4b-5163-ba35-f70ec792f91d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8680e3ab-ac4b-5163-ba35-f70ec792f91d" "answer-82bca19e-14cc-56cc-9397-e33111aae553" "answer-8c8f1b4f-ea6f-50a7-90b7-28a18c762dfe" "answer-f5c9c363-73dc-5320-b19f-2ebf3f0d2405" "answer-a1f552c7-b78f-5465-9564-878cf6243fe9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8680e3ab-ac4b-5163-ba35-f70ec792f91d" :answer/id #uuid "8680e3ab-ac4b-5163-ba35-f70ec792f91d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82bca19e-14cc-56cc-9397-e33111aae553" :answer/id #uuid "82bca19e-14cc-56cc-9397-e33111aae553" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c8f1b4f-ea6f-50a7-90b7-28a18c762dfe" :answer/id #uuid "8c8f1b4f-ea6f-50a7-90b7-28a18c762dfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5c9c363-73dc-5320-b19f-2ebf3f0d2405" :answer/id #uuid "f5c9c363-73dc-5320-b19f-2ebf3f0d2405" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1f552c7-b78f-5465-9564-878cf6243fe9" :answer/id #uuid "a1f552c7-b78f-5465-9564-878cf6243fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345167 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 25 & -25\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ 25{x}_{3}=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+3(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(-1)-(-1)=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186344579 :answer-field/choices ["answer-5de78ea6-b293-58dc-961e-a74b7da29c90"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5de78ea6-b293-58dc-961e-a74b7da29c90" :answer/id #uuid "5de78ea6-b293-58dc-961e-a74b7da29c90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120358 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 0=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the fourth equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186318899 :answer-field/correct "answer-c12d4923-cf32-5625-bd6b-336210c2bb42" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c12d4923-cf32-5625-bd6b-336210c2bb42"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c12d4923-cf32-5625-bd6b-336210c2bb42" :answer/id #uuid "c12d4923-cf32-5625-bd6b-336210c2bb42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121042 :tutorial/content "Given a subspace $H$ with a basis $\\mathcal B = \\{ \\mathbf b_1, \\mathbf b_2 \\}$ and a vector $\\mathbf x \\in H,$ the **coordinates of the vector** $\\mathbf{x}$ **relative to the basis** $\\mathcal{B}$ are the coefficients ${\\color{red} x_1}$ and ${\\color{blue} x_2}$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}x_1} \\mathbf{b}_1+{\\color{blue}x_2} \\mathbf{b}_2 = \\mathbf{x}.\n$$\n\nWe can write the vector $\\mathbf x$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal B$ using these coordinates, as follows:\n\n![](images/05/0593ca6a838b66c4623e8749eb5236d6259b1f9bf36ed0d68b83c49781076341.svg)\n\nTo demonstrate, consider the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where \n\n![](images/f3/f355faa0c477775f2a1cbb3522d0743cdbc9649a5ee9c55b579b1fac9ae2a661.svg)\n\nAlso let $H = \\textrm{span} \\{ \\mathbf b_1, \\mathbf b_2 \\},$ and consider the vector ![](images/78/78357fcf51c9cd6b7873f5bc35fcc214cb3790bcec00ee69d0932f15aacd39cb.svg)\n\nThe vector $\\mathbf x$ can be expressed as a unique linear combination of $\\mathbf b_1$ and $\\mathbf b_2.$ That is to say, there exist *unique coefficients* $\\color{red}x_1$ and $\\color{blue}x_2$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's solve for these coefficients. From the above, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of this system is \n\n![](images/82/82d4f494936d23e9b697aa4518edf68f7ea62e504d9d2576a6d13971acaf1c96.svg)\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = {\\color{red}3} \\mathbf{b}_1+ {\\color{blue}2} \\mathbf{b}_2,\n$$\n\nwhich can be visualized as shown below.\n\n![](images/94/94b2934727a32284e9790e59ccd301bd858a0258843314a2968285a5eda7a302.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121066 :tutorial/content "Let's consider a set of vectors\n![](images/0d/0d78e1b2d01003885882f19b3856278e5024719f26f33594fd071fbd73273b71.svg)\n\nNotice that the set $\\mathcal{S}$ is linearly independent since the vector equation $x_1\\mathbf{e}_1+x_2\\mathbf{e}_2+x_3\\mathbf{e}_3=\\mathbf{0}$ leads to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has only the zero solution. \n\nAlso, notice that any vector in $\\mathbb{R}^3$ can be written as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{e}_1,$ $\\mathbf{e}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{e}_3.$ For instance,\n![](images/ef/ef28dd8cbad6d256b9fa82c487263af3327ce630839cfcd1c7433417d0e0ae73.svg)\n\nIn particular, the equation above tells us that \n![](images/72/724f42afb534edbde7588c5508a4bf8de6d3cd068bc2989da7c7207b1bf7a1ba.svg)\nthat is to say, the numbers $\\color{red}-2,$ $\\color{red}0,$ $\\color{red}5$ are the coordinates of $\\mathbf{v}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{S}.$ \n\nThe basis $\\mathcal{S}$ is somewhat special, since the coordinates of a vector relative to this basis coincide with the components of the vector. We refer to $\\mathcal{S}$ as the **standard basis**. Remember that in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and $\\mathbb{R}^3$ we even have special notations for the vectors of the standard basis:\n![](images/ae/aee5dd3226ebe950defc8b873399a884e0679ce701a3a55354ef01960e029f8e.svg)\n\n![](images/dd/dd96e0b70173adf8983feb4975c351ab3e417c34ed4a6a944bc391e33db4c8e9.png)\n\nIn general, the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ is\n\n![](images/a8/a8e4b648898c0dc036e228fb84945833dc40c053beff034596e098c4dd077e23.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}]
